    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** (72.55) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.72) headline our active roster as the clear primary targets. **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Buehler (4.56 xERA) and a massive 13% boost from his platoon dynamic, making him our highest-projected start. Meanwhile, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start despite facing a tough arm in Cole (3.76 xERA); he retains his elite status thanks to a strong BvP historical edge (8% bump) and a premium spot in the two-hole. We are also capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups for **Lawrence Butler** (69.19) and **Tyler Freeman** (67.98), both of whom take advantage of exploitable SPs and advantageous batting order positioning to comfortably clear our 60-point \"Strong\" threshold.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved our bench, where **Gleyber Torres** (49.99) narrowly missed the final cut. While **Gleyber Torres** possesses an appealing order slot, his negative platoon split against Martinez and park factors pushed him just below the efficiency of our starting outfielders. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** (47.47) was sidelined by a difficult matchup against Ohtani, whose 2.99 xERA severely suppresses the offensive floor for left-handed hitters. We have intentionally benched **Gavin Sheets** (38.57) due to his failure to meet the 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold, and we continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL. Managers should keep a close eye on **Masyn Winn**, as his score of 51.23 is buoyed largely by his leadoff status despite the risk associated with facing Gore (3.91 xERA); he remains a high-variance play where his sprint speed for stolen bases is the primary driver of his inclusion over deeper bench options.",
